Local accepted the shape of the table: the billing mode, the on-demand maximum, both indexes (including `byMerchant`'s key of three attributes), the stream, and deletion protection, which then refused the `delete-table`. It accepted the warm throughput but reports `null`, because there's nothing to warm in one program. Point-in-time recovery is an unknown operation: the docs list it as unsupported in Local. TTL is accepted, but in the run behind this lesson an item that had expired ten minutes earlier was still there. So don't use Local to test when TTL deletes happen.
